(  on_abort.ngc - task-level abort cleanup for the Mazak ATC remap.        )
(                                                                          )
(  Wired via [RS274NGC]ON_ABORT_COMMAND in mazak_vqc_20_40.ini. Called by  )
(  LinuxCNC's task subsystem whenever program execution is aborted for    )
(  any of the reasons enumerated in nml_intf/emc.hh:                       )
(                                                                          )
(    1  EMC_ABORT_TASK_EXEC_ERROR                                          )
(    2  EMC_ABORT_AUX_ESTOP                                                )
(    3  EMC_ABORT_MOTION_OR_IO_RCS_ERROR                                   )
(    4  EMC_ABORT_TASK_STATE_OFF                                           )
(    5  EMC_ABORT_TASK_STATE_ESTOP_RESET                                   )
(    6  EMC_ABORT_TASK_STATE_ESTOP                                         )
(    7  EMC_ABORT_TASK_STATE_NOT_ON                                        )
(    8  EMC_ABORT_TASK_ABORT      (operator Abort button / halui.abort)    )
(    9  EMC_ABORT_INTERPRETER_ERROR                                        )
(   10  EMC_ABORT_INTERPRETER_ERROR_MDI                                    )
(  100+ EMC_ABORT_USER                                                     )
(                                                                          )
(  Reference: LinuxCNC remap docs                                          )
(    https://linuxcnc.org/docs/html/remap/remap.html                       )
(  and INI reference                                                       )
(    https://linuxcnc.org/docs/html/config/ini-config.html                 )
(                                                                          )
(  Cause code lands in the single positional parameter #1.                 )
(                                                                          )
(  This routine performs a MECHANICALLY SAFE ordered drop of the ATC and  )
(  orient interlocks. The order matters: dropping the barrier or magazine )
(  cover request before the tool-clamp path can leave the head hanging   )
(  from a partially-clamped tool. Sequence:                                )
(                                                                          )
(    1. Pulse P8 (atc-cycle-abort) high so mazak_atc.comp and             )
(       mazak_orient.comp latch !cycle_active on the current servo cycle. )
(       The comps' internal abort/reset paths (see mazak_atc.comp line 355 )
(       and mazak_orient.comp line 274) then drop atc_barrier,            )
(       mag_cover_sol, tool_unclamp_sol, mag_fwd/rev_sol, spindle_orient  )
(       outputs in one consistent step, subject to permissives.           )
(                                                                          )
(    2. Explicitly drop each of P0..P7 in the same order the remap        )
(       normally uses on a clean cycle exit. This is belt-and-suspenders  )
(       - if the comp did not see the P8 pulse in time (e.g. abort at    )
(       step 1 before the cycle_active latch even set), the outputs go    )
(       to their safe rest state anyway.                                  )
(                                                                          )
(    3. Drop P8 so the comp can accept a new cycle_start on the next M6. )
(                                                                          )
(  ORDERING (index-critical):                                              )
(    a. P4 - detect-check first: it is a diagnostic gate, safe to drop.   )
(    b. P5 - cycle-finish drops (won't trigger anything on a clean state).)
(    c. P2 - unclamp-request drops FIRST among the clamp-family so the   )
(       tool_unclamp_sol goes de-energised via the comp's next tick,     )
(       relying on the spring-clamp to keep the tool held. mazak_atc.comp )
(       already gates the unclamp_sol on !faulted and !cycle_abort.       )
(    d. P3 - magazine index request drops so the magazine motor stops.   )
(    e. P6 - orient-request drops.                                        )
(    f. P7 - orient-cancel pulsed high then low to force the orient comp )
(       to its idle state. mazak_orient.comp treats orient_cancel as a   )
(       hard reset independent of orient_request.                         )
(    g. P1 - cover-close-request drops LAST because the magazine cover   )
(       is the physical guard; leaving it in its previous commanded      )
(       state until every rotating element is idle is the safe order.    )
(    h. P0 - cycle-active drops last, releasing the barrier.              )
(                                                                          )
(  This runs OUTSIDE a cycle context so it uses no G53 moves. If motion  )
(  was in-flight when the abort fired, the task subsystem has already    )
(  issued its own motion abort - this proc only cleans up digital I/O   )
(  and comp state.                                                        )
(                                                                          )

o<on_abort> sub

  (DEBUG, on_abort cleanup entered, cause=#1)

  ( Step 1: pulse atc-cycle-abort so the comps drop their state cleanly )
  M64 P8
  G4 P0.050              ( 50 ms - well over one servo cycle at 1 kHz )

  ( Step 2: safe-ordered explicit drop of P0..P7 )
  M65 P4                 ( detect-check disarm )
  M65 P5                 ( cycle-finish drop )
  M65 P2                 ( unclamp-request drop - releases tool_unclamp_sol )
  M65 P3                 ( magazine index-request drop )
  M65 P6                 ( orient-request drop )

  ( Force orient into cancel state - orient_cancel is a hard reset )
  M64 P7                 ( orient-cancel high )
  G4 P0.020              ( 20 ms - long enough for one comp tick )
  M65 P7                 ( orient-cancel back low )

  M65 P1                 ( cover-close-request drop - cover stays where it is )
  M65 P0                 ( cycle-active drop - releases atc_barrier )

  ( Step 3: drop atc-cycle-abort so the next cycle can start clean )
  G4 P0.050              ( 50 ms guard so comps see the abort while outputs settle )
  M65 P8

  (DEBUG, on_abort cleanup complete)

o<on_abort> endsub
